  seo_title, seo_description, reading_minutes, cta, created_at, updated_at)
values ('How Much Does SEO Cost for a Small Business in 2026?', 'how-much-does-seo-cost-small-business-2026', 'What small businesses typically pay for SEO, what drives the price, the pricing models agencies use and how to judge whether a quote is worth it.', '“How much does SEO cost?” is one of the first questions business owners ask, and one of the hardest to answer in a sentence. The honest answer depends on your market, your website and what you want SEO to achieve. Here''s how to think about it — and how to tell a fair quote from a risky one.', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"what-you-pay-for"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What you''re actually paying for"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SEO isn''t one task. A typical engagement combines technical work (site speed, indexing, structured data), on-page work (making service and product pages match what people search for), content creation and authority building. Some months lean technical; others lean content."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The more of these your site needs — and the more competitive your market — the more effort it takes to move results. A five-page local business site with clean code needs far less work than a five-thousand-product store with duplicate content and slow templates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You''re also paying for judgment: deciding which keywords are worth chasing, which pages to fix first and which work to skip entirely. Good prioritization is often the difference between SEO that pays for itself and SEO that just produces reports."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"pricing-models"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Common SEO pricing models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most agencies and consultants use one of these models:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Monthly retainer: ongoing work for a fixed fee. The most common model for small businesses."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"One-time audit or project: a technical audit, a site migration or a fixed set of fixes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hourly consulting: useful if your team will do the implementation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Performance-based pricing: paid per ranking or lead. Be careful — it can encourage shortcuts that put your site at risk."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"typical-ranges"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Typical price ranges"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As a rough guide, small-business SEO retainers in the US, UK, Canada and Australia often fall somewhere between about $500 and $5,000 per month, with one-time audits ranging from a few hundred to a few thousand dollars. Local businesses in less competitive areas tend toward the lower end; e-commerce stores and businesses in competitive cities toward the higher end."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Teams based in lower-cost countries, including India, can often deliver similar work for less — but price alone tells you little about quality. What matters is what''s included and how results are measured."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Treat any figure you see online, including these, as a starting point for conversation rather than a benchmark. Two quotes at the same price can contain very different amounts of real work."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"what-drives-cost"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What drives the cost up or down"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The biggest factors are:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Competition: ranking for “personal injury lawyer” in a major city takes far more work than for a niche service in a small town."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Site condition: a slow site with technical issues needs fixing before content can perform."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope: one location versus many; fifty products versus five thousand."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Content needs: how much new content is needed, and who writes it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Who implements changes: if your SEO provider can''t edit your website, every fix waits on a developer."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"whats-included"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What a fair quote should include"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A good SEO proposal is specific. It should tell you what will be done in the first few months, how priorities were chosen, who does the work and how progress will be reported. Look for these elements:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A technical audit with a prioritized fix list, not a 100-page export from a tool"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyword and competitor research tied to your services or products"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A content plan with realistic volume and clear ownership"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversion tracking, so SEO is judged by inquiries and sales"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A reporting rhythm and a clear way to end the engagement"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"red-flags"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Red flags in SEO quotes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Be cautious of guaranteed rankings (nobody controls Google), very cheap packages promising hundreds of backlinks, vague monthly reports with no business outcomes, and contracts that lock you in for a year with no exit."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Also be wary of providers who won''t explain what they''re doing. Legitimate SEO has nothing to hide; you should be able to see every change made to your site and every piece of content published."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"how-to-budget"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"How to set your SEO budget"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Work backward from value. Estimate what a new customer is worth to you, how many extra customers per month would make SEO worthwhile, and how long you can invest before expecting returns — usually several months."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need results this month, pair SEO with paid search. Ads bring traffic immediately and show which searches convert, which helps focus your SEO."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2,"id":"bottom-line"},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bottom line"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good SEO is an investment in an asset — rankings and content that keep working. Choose a provider who explains exactly what they''ll do, measures success in leads and sales, and can fix your website themselves when it''s holding you back."}]}]}'::jsonb, 'Pytron Digital Team',
  (select id from public.blog_categories where slug = 'seo'), 'PUBLISHED', '2026-10-04T12:59:00Z',
  '', '', 3, 'marketing',
  '2026-10-04T12:59:00Z', '2026-10-04T12:59:00Z')
